  <text id="shot-label" x="74" y="154" width="528" height="14" font="caption" size="11" color="muted" align="center" wrap="false">Real application screenshot • field mission workflow with low-connectivity, evidence, and sync-aware execution</text>

  <shape id="card1" type="rect" x="654" y="146" width="568" height="122" fill="surface" stroke="border" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="card1t" x="680" y="170" width="516" height="76" font="body" size="18" color="ink" line-height="1.3"><p><strong color="brand-green">Demarcation continuity</strong></p><p space-before="10">Field officers can continue parcel checks and demarcation-sensitive work without losing continuity between site activity and the digital case record.</p></text>

  <shape id="card2" type="rect" x="654" y="292" width="568" height="122" fill="surface" stroke="border" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="card2t" x="680" y="316" width="516" height="76" font="body" size="18" color="ink" line-height="1.3"><p><strong color="brand-green">Evidence photography and proof handling</strong></p><p space-before="10">Ownership evidence, parcel notes, and site observations remain connected to the case, supporting stronger verification discipline.</p></text>

  <shape id="card3" type="rect" x="654" y="438" width="568" height="136" fill="surface" stroke="border" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="card3t" x="680" y="462" width="516" height="88" font="body" size="18" color="ink" line-height="1.3"><p><strong color="brand-green">Low-connectivity replay and registry alignment</strong></p><p space-before="10">Queued field events, offline continuity, and reconciliation controls help Kano preserve a reliable bridge between site work and the official registry flow.</p></text>

